window.MONSTER_CHUNK_149 = [{"name":"Woolly Rhinoceros Elasmotherium","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"animal","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+10 natural, -1 size","hp":172,"hd":"15d8+105","hdvalue":15,"fort":17,"ref":9,"will":6,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"gore +21 (2d6+15/19-20)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"powerful charge","details":"gore, 8d6+24"},{"type":"trample","details":"1d6+15, DC 27"}],"strength":31,"dexterity":10,"constitution":23,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":13,"charisma":2,"baseatk":11,"cmb":22,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","cmd":32,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (gore)"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (gore)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":25}],"environments":["cold forests","any marshes","any plains","temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary","herd (2-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature has massive legs and a stout body with a thick coat of brown fur. From the tip of its elongated nose rise two curving horns.","group":"Rhinoceros","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"The elasmotherium stands as tall and as long as an elephant, averaging almost 15 ft. long and weighing around four tons. Its fur is thick, and its underlying body is tough and very resilient. Its single horn is thick, ivory colored, and almost six feet long.\n\nIts fur tends to be a bit darker than the common woolly rhino's. Like its brethren, its eyesight is poor, thus it too relies on its keen sense of hearing and smell. The elasmotherium is a herding creature and encounters with herds are common. When danger presents itself, the females encircle the young, while the males charge the predator, goring with its horn."},{"name":"Ancient Dungeon Dragon","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["shapechanger"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (300 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":35,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":35,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +28 natural, -2 size","hp":218,"hd":"19d12+95","hdvalue":19,"fort":16,"ref":10,"will":18,"dr":"15/magic","immunities":["enchantment spells and effects","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +28 (2d8+16), 2 claws +28 (2d6+11), 2 wings +26 (1d8+5), tail slap +26 (2d6+16)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100 ft. line or 50 ft. cone, DC 25, confusion 1d6 rounds"},{"type":"crush"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":19,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":24,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"},{"spell":"mass suggestion"},{"spell":"suggestion"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":14,"spellsknown_concentration":19,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":7,"spell_slots":3,"spells":[{"spell":"mass hold person"}]},{"spell_level":6,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"antimagic field"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"}]},{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"persistent image"},{"spell":"prying eyes"},{"spell":"teleport"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane eye"},{"spell":"detect scrying"},{"spell":"illusory wall"},{"spell":"lesser globe of invulnerability"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane sight"},{"spell":"deep slumber"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"major image"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane lock"},{"spell":"magic mouth"},{"spell":"make whole"},{"spell":"phantom trap"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"hold portal"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"silent image"},{"spell":"ventriloquism"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"daze"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":33,"dexterity":9,"constitution":20,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":20,"charisma":18,"baseatk":19,"cmb":32,"cmd":41,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Craft Wondrous Item","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Master Craftsman","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Bluff)"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Craft [crystal carving])"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Knowledge [engineering])"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":32},{"skill":"Craft (crystal carving)","value":24},{"skill":"Craft (traps)","value":17},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":21},{"skill":"Disable Device","value":14},{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":6},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (engineering)","value":33},{"skill":"Linguistics","value":27},{"skill":"Perception","value":35},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":31},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":27}],"languages":["24 languages (except Druidic)","plus Common and Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape","details":"alter self"},{"type":"craft crystal ball"}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple standard plus crystal ball","description_visual":"This dragon has a long serpentine neck, small wings, and glistening scales. Two small horns dominate its triangular head. Its body is gray in color, with scales tipped in flecks of gold and green. Its eyes are rounded and gray.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A dungeon dragon's breath weapon is a line or cone of warm mist. Creatures caught in the area must succeed on Fortitude save or be affected as if by a confusion spell for 1d6 rounds."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"At will, a very young or older dungeon dragon can assume the form of any Small or Medium humanoid creature (as the alter self spell). It can remain in its humanoid form indefinitely. It cannot take the form of a specific individual."},{"type":"Craft Crystal Ball","kind":"Ex","details":"Dungeon dragon parents begin teaching their wyrmlings the necessary skills and spells to craft a crystal ball soon after they leave the egg. A dungeon dragon gains the Master Craftsman feat for free as a bonus feat without having to meet the prerequisites."},{"type":"Craft Wondrous Item","kind":"Ex","details":"Older dungeon dragons create new crystal balls with additional powers as they grow in intelligence and spellcasting ability. A young adult dungeon dragon gains the Craft Wondrous Item feat for free as a bonus feat."},{"type":"Dominate Monster","kind":"Sp","details":"A great wyrm dungeon dragon can use this ability three times per day. It works as a dominate monster spell. This ability is the equivalent of an 8th-level spell. Skills Dungeon dragons gain a +4 bonus to Perception checks. Spell-like Abilities A dungeon dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Young-charm person; Juvenile-detect thoughts; Adult-suggestion; Old-charm monster; Ancient-mass suggestion; Great Wyrm-mass charm monster. The dungeon dragon uses these abilities to populate its dungeon with monsters it encounters in the surrounding terrain."}],"description":"The dungeon dragon is a curious creature that gets amusement by watching other beings engaged in life and death struggles. To this end, a dungeon dragon sets up a labyrinthine lair, setting traps and populating it with monsters. Younger dungeon dragons tend to lair in natural caverns to ease the burden of construction. Older, more experienced dungeon dragons have been known to construct their own sprawling subterranean complexes, even to the point of hiring on dwarf work gangs and swearing them to secrecy. Once the construction and refurbishing of its lair is complete, the dungeon dragon transforms itself into a humanoid and ventures into the surrounding countryside.\n\nThere it spreads rumors and tales of this horrible catacomb in hopes of luring adventurers forth so it may watch them via its crystal ball. Young dungeon dragons often spend years living among humanoids, even to the point of joining adventurers involved in dungeon delves. On such adventures, the intrepid dungeon dragon takes notes regarding the devious traps and monsters it encounters so that it can add such things to its own lair. Oddly enough, although a dungeon dragon goes to great pains to amass a treasure hoard, it cares little for material wealth. Rather, it uses the treasure it gathers as bait in its dungeon to lure in adventurers and provide it the entertainment it so greatly desires.\n\nWatching adventurers explore its catacomb is the only real treasure a dungeon dragon desires. The only material possession a dungeon dragon will risk its life to save is its crystal ball. Without this vital piece of equipment, all of the dragon's labor is in vain. A dungeon dragon in its natural form prefers to flee any combat. It likes to watch other creatures engaged in fights for life, not itself. If forced into melee, it swats at opponents with its powerful claws and bite. A dungeon dragon is proficient in the use of all simple and martial weapons and light and medium armor and shields."},{"name":"Chalkydri","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"NG","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["angel","extraplanar","good"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect evil"},{"type":"see invisibility"}],"auras":["protective aura"],"ac":30,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +13 natural, +4 sacred | +4 deflection vs. evil","hp":126,"hd":"12d10+60","hdvalue":12,"fort":13,"ref":11,"will":10,"save_mods":"+4 vs. poison, +4 vs. evil","dr":"10/evil","immunities":["acid","cold","petrification","death effects"],"resists":[{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":90,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+2 flaming longsword +21 (1d8+8 plus 1d6 fire)","ranged":"+2 flaming javelin +17 (1d6+8 plus 1d6 fire)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect evil"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"aid"},{"spell":"bless"},{"spell":"consecrate"},{"spell":"continual flame"},{"spell":"discern lies"},{"spell":"dispel evil"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"holy smite"},{"spell":"invisibility","details":"self only"},{"spell":"plane shift"},{"spell":"remove curse"},{"spell":"remove disease"},{"spell":"remove fear"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"heal"},{"spell":"raise dead"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 8, 1d4 movanic devas 35%"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"atonement"},{"spell":"cure serious wounds"},{"spell":"flame strike"},{"spell":"greater restoration"},{"spell":"holy word"},{"spell":"polymorph","details":"self only"}]}],"strength":23,"dexterity":16,"constitution":20,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":18,"charisma":19,"baseatk":12,"cmb":18,"cmd":35,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (longsword)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":19},{"skill":"Fly","value":22},{"skill":"Heal","value":19},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":19},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":16},{"skill":"Perception","value":23},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":23},{"skill":"Stealth","value":18},{"skill":"Survival","value":19}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic","Infernal","truespeech"],"environments":["any good-aligned plane"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This angelic-looking creature resembles a muscular humanoid with coppery skin and coppery eyes. It has four large feathery wings of white and carries a longsword swathed in fire.","group":"Angel","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"Chalkydris spend most of their time on the Ethereal or Astral Plane or on one of the many Elemental Planes, usually acting on behalf of some deity of good. Chalkydris are militaristic and often lead small retinues of other celestials against the infernal armies. When not serving in such roles, they are found acting as protectors or escorts to visitors on the good-aligned planes. Sometimes, a chalkydri is sent to the Material Plane by its deity to watch over a favored worshipper. When traveling the Material Plane, the chalkydri often takes a form more acceptable to humanoids.\n\nChalkydris appear as powerful, agile humans 6 to 7 ft. tall with coppery skin, red or blonde hair, and copper-colored eyes. Two sets of large feathery wings (four wings total) protrude from their back at shoulder level. Their wings are glossy white with copper tips. Chalkydris wear tunics or robes of varying colors, usually crimson, copper, green, silver, or gold.\n\nChalkydris enjoy combat and one is never without its +2 flaming longsword and at least two +2 flaming javelins. A chalkydri opens combat by hurling one of its javelins at a foe before moving into melee to battle with its longsword. While in combat, it utilizes its spell-like abilities to their fullest extent. If a chalkydri is overwhelmed in battle, it summons celestials to its aid or uses its plane shift ability to escape. If slain, the chalkydri's weapons explode in a blinding flash of fire.","gear":"+2 flaming longsword, 2 +2 flaming javelins"},{"name":"Dark Matter Entropic Ooze","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"ooze","subtypes":["extraplanar"],"init":-3,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"soulsight","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":13,"ac_touch":5,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"-3 Dex, +8 natural, -2 size","hp":391,"hd":"27d8+270","hdvalue":27,"fort":19,"ref":6,"will":9,"save_mods":"Will: +2 vs. charm effects","immunities":["negative energy","ooze traits"],"sr":24,"sr_mods":"vs. positive energy","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"climb","speed":20}],"melee":"slam +28 (2d8+15 plus energy drain)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"devour soul"},{"type":"energy drain","details":"3 levels, DC 23"}],"strength":31,"dexterity":4,"constitution":30,"wisdom":1,"charisma":10,"baseatk":20,"cmb":32,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":18}],"environments":["any (Plane of Negative Energy)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This protoplasmic creature resembles a giant amoeba, black in color. A deathly cold seems to emanate from its form.","group":"Ooze","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Devour Soul","kind":"Su","details":"A living creature slain by an entropic ooze has its soul devoured by the ooze. Such a creature cannot be returned to life until the entropic ooze that contains its soul is slain."},{"type":"Soulsight","kind":"Su","details":"An entropic ooze can automatically detect the location of any living creature within 120 ft. It also senses the strength of their life force automatically, as if it had cast deathwatch."}],"description":"A larger, more powerful version of the standard entropic ooze is know as the dark matter entropic ooze, a massive creature that rarely leaves its home plane. Spellcasters who summon this creature often live (or don't live) to regret it."},{"name":"Furnace Golem","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"construct","init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":29,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":29,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +22 natural, -2 size","hp":144,"hd":"19d10+40","hdvalue":19,"fort":6,"ref":5,"will":6,"dr":"15/adamantine","immunities":["construct traits","fire","magic","rust"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":20}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"2 slams +28 (4d6+11 plus 2d6 fire plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50-ft. line, 10d6 fire, Reflex DC 19 half, every 1d4 rounds"},{"type":"furnace-interior"},{"type":"heat"}],"strength":32,"dexterity":9,"wisdom":11,"charisma":1,"baseatk":19,"cmb":32,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":41,"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This 20-foot tall construct looks like a humanoid clad in black iron armor. A large grate-covered opening in its abdomen houses a roaring fire in its innards.","group":"Golem","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Furnace-Interior","kind":"Ex","details":"A furnace golem can try to shove a grabbed opponent up to two sizes smaller than itself into its interior by making a successful grapple check. An opponent thrown into the furnace golem's interior is trapped as a metal grating closes over the opening in the same round. A trapped creature automatically takes 2d6 points of fire damage each round. Escaping the creature's interior requires a successful Strength check (DC 30) to bend the bars. Alternately a trapped creature can escape by dealing at least 25 points of damage to the bars (AC 22). Note, the golem's damage reduction applies to all attacks against the bars. A Huge furnace golem's interior can hold 2 Medium, 8 Small, or 16 Tiny or smaller creatures."},{"type":"Heat","kind":"Ex","details":"A furnace golem's entire form is extremely hot. Any slam attack deals fire damage. Creatures attacking a furnace golem unarmed or with natural weapons take this same fire damage each time one of their attacks hits."},{"type":"Immunity to Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"A furnace golem is immune to any spell or spell-like ability that allows spell resistance. In addition, certain spells and effects function differently against the creature as noted below. A magical attack that bypasses its cold resistance slows a furnace golem (as the slow spell) for 3 rounds, with no saving throw. A magical attack that deals fire damage breaks any slow effect on the furnace golem and heals 1 point of damage for each 3 points of damage the attack would otherwise deal. If the amount of damage would cause the golem to exceed its full normal hit points, it gains any excess as temporary hit points."}],"description":"Furnace golems are most often used to guard some arcane secret or treasure, though some are programmed to seek out objects or individuals. Those used as guards stand motionless, appearing as nothing more than a giant black iron statue, until activated. Furnace golems, like other constructs, obey their creator's commands to the best of their ability. Should the creator die, or should the golem's commands be unattainable, the furnace golem becomes rogue.\n\nThat is, it is still completely functional but follows no commands or orders from anyone. Furnace golems open combat using their breath weapon before moving to pulverize their opponents with their massive fists. Grabbed opponents are shoved into the golem's burning interior where they are trapped until they break free or die. The fires powering a furnace golem are magical in nature, i.e. it needs no source of natural fuel to power it and they cannot be extinguished, though if a furnace golem is destroyed, the fires in its innards burn out.\n\n**CONSTRUCTION**\nA furnace golem's body is constructed from 8,000 pounds of iron mixed with rare ingredients and chemicals totaling 12,000 gp.\n\nFURNACE GOLEM; CL 16th; Price 180,000 gp\nConstruction Requirements: Craft Construct, fireball, geas/quest, limited wish, polymorph any object, wall of fire, creator must be caster level 16th; Skill Craft (armor or weapons) DC 20; Cost 96,000 gp"},{"name":"Gharros Demon","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":28,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +15 natural, -1 size","hp":248,"hd":"16d10+160","hdvalue":16,"fort":20,"ref":14,"will":9,"dr":"15/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"battleaxe +25 (2d6+10/19-20/x3) or battleaxe +25 (2d6+10/19-20/x3), 2 stings +26 (1d8+10/19- 20 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":22,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"darkness"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"mirror image"},{"spell":"telekinesis"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 6, 4d10 dretches, 1d4 vrocks, or 1d2 glabrezus 50%; or 1 gharros 20%"}]}],"strength":31,"dexterity":18,"constitution":30,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":18,"charisma":20,"baseatk":16,"cmb":27,"cmd":41,"cmd_special":"+8 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (battleaxe)"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (tail sting)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (sting)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":14},{"skill":"Bluff","value":24},{"skill":"Climb","value":29},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":21},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":15},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13},{"skill":"Survival","value":23}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common","any three","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","pack (2-4)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This hideous creature appears to be half-scorpion and half-human. Its upper torso is that of a greenish-silver humanoid with long, flowing dark hair and stark white eyes while its lower torso is that of a reddish-brown scorpion. Its tail splits into two separate stingers and the creature's mouth is filled with razor-sharp teeth.","group":"Demon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Sting-injury; save Fort DC 28; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Con damage; cure 1 save."}],"description":"A gharros looks like a cross between a large human and an even larger scorpion. They serve as guards, soldiers, shock troops (and even assassins sometimes) to some of the minor nobles and lesser demon lords of the Abyss. They hate all goodness and seek to destroy it at any opportunity through whatever means available.\n\nA gharros is about 8 ft. tall and 10 ft. long and weighs around 1,500 pounds.\n\nGharros are very aggressive in battle and seek to kill the strongest opponent first. They wield their battleaxes in combat and sting with their deadly tails, all the while sprinkling the fight with their spell-like abilities.\n\nUnless ordered to do so, gharros never take prisoners in battle. They fight to the death (either their death or their opponent's).","gear":"battleaxe"},{"name":"Noble Time Elemental","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","time"],"init":9,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge, +4 insight, +6 natural, -1 size","hp":190,"hd":"20d10+80","hdvalue":20,"fort":10,"ref":19,"will":18,"defensive_abilities":["foresight"],"dr":"15/-","immunities":["elemental traits","temporal magic"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":20,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +24 (2d6+4)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"alter age","details":"1/day, Fort DC 24"},{"type":"multi-manifestation"},{"type":"temporal displacement","details":"3/day, 20 minutes, Fort DC 24"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":24,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"time stop"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":20,"constitution":18,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":18,"charisma":15,"baseatk":20,"cmb":25,"cmd":45,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (slam)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":22},{"skill":"Fly","value":34},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":27},{"skill":"Perception","value":33},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":27},{"skill":"Stealth","value":24},{"skill":"Survival","value":27}],"languages":["telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"time jaunt","details":"Will DC 24"}],"environments":["any (Plane of Time)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (noble plus 1-2 common time elementals)","court (royal plus 1-2 nobles and 1-4 common time elementals)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears as a formless cloud of yellowish-red vapor or dust about 5 ft. in diameter.","group":"Elemental","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Alter Age","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day, a noble time elemental can age a creature simply by touching it (this requires a melee touch attack). If successful, the target must succeed on a Fortitude save or advance forward one aging step (from adulthood to middle age, from middle age to old, from old to venerable, and so on). If a character ages, he takes all the effects to his physical ability scores, but doesn't gain any of the bonuses to his mental ability scores. A venerable creature affected by this ability dies (from massive cell death) and cannot be restored to life by mortal magic. The save DC is Constitution-based. Alternately, a time elemental can use its alter age ability to reduce a character's age. If the target is unwilling, the time elemental must succeed on a melee touch attack. An unwilling target can make a Fortitude save to avoid the effects. If the save fails, the target ages one age step backwards (from middle age to adulthood for example) and gains all bonuses to physical ability scores from his new age (simply flip the penalties listed on the aging table into an equal numbered bonus). A character that regresses in age doesn't reduce its mental ability scores. This ability doesn't affect a character that has died from old age. A time elemental can also use this ability to age vegetable matter 10-200 years (older or younger) or mineral matter 100-2,000 years (older or younger). Royal time elementals can use this ability twice per day."},{"type":"Cell Death","kind":"Ex","details":"Damage dealt by a time elemental's slam attack doesn't heal naturally (but it can still be healed magically). Additionally, a creature slain by a time elemental can only be raised through the successful casting of a miracle, true resurrection, or wish spell."},{"type":"Foresight","kind":"Su","details":"A time elemental can see a few seconds into the future. This ability prevents it from being surprised, caught flat-footed, or flanked. It also grants the time elemental an insight bonus to AC equal to its Wisdom bonus. This ability can be negated, but the time elemental can restart it as a free action on its next turn."},{"type":"Immunity to Temporal Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"Time elementals are immune to all time-related spells and effects (including time stop, temporal stasis, and the like). Note, the time stop ability of the noble and royal time elementals can affect those time elementals of lesser power (i.e., a noble can affect a common and a royal can affect a noble or common)."},{"type":"Multi-Manifestation","kind":"Su","details":"A time elemental exists in several other dimensions at any given time. As a standard action, it can bring forth 1d4 of these manifestations to its current locale in order to gain multiple attacks that round. Treat each manifestation as a separate time elemental with hit points equal to the time elemental's current hit points. A manifestation cannot use any of the supernatural or spell-like abilities of the time elemental (a manifestation does however gain the time elemental's foresight ability). A time elemental cannot have more than four manifestations present at one time. Because each manifestation is a part of the time elemental that called them, a successful attack on the time elemental or any of its manifestations deals an equal amount of damage to them all."},{"type":"Summon Time Elementals","kind":"Sp","details":"Once per day, a royal time elemental can attempt to summon 1d4 common time elementals with a 70% chance of success or 1-2 noble time elementals with a 30% chance of success. This ability is the equivalent of a 9th-level spell."},{"type":"Temporal Displacement","kind":"Su","details":"By making a melee touch attack against a foe, a noble or royal time elemental can remove that creature from the current time stream if it fails a Fortitude save. The save is Constitution-based. On a failed save, the creature disappears in a flash of white energy. For a number of minutes equal to the time elemental's Hit Dice, the displaced creature is effectively nonexistent. No form of magic, effect, or force can detect or aid such a creature. A displaced creature can attempt a Wisdom check (DC equal to the initial Fort DC) on its turn to break the effects and end the displacement. The save is Constitution-based. When the effect ends, the creature reappears in the same space it was in before being displaced. If the space is occupied when the creature returns, it is shunted aside to the first open space and takes no damage. A noble or royal time elemental can use this ability three times per day."},{"type":"Time Jaunt","kind":"Su","details":"A time elemental can slip through the time stream and appear anywhere on the same plane of existence as if by greater teleport. This ability transports the time elemental and up to four other creatures within a 30-foot radius. Unwilling creatures can attempt a Will save to avoid being carried away. This ability is otherwise similar to the spell of the same name (caster level equal to the elemental's HD). The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Time Stop","kind":"Sp","details":"Noble and royal time elementals can create an effect identical to a time stop spell once per day (caster level equals the time elemental's HD)."}],"description":"Time elementals are creatures from a plane most sages are unaware even exists. A time elemental is a powerful creature formed of pure time and matter such as is unknown to even the most learned of sages. It is unknown how or why time elementals enter the Material Plane, as they cannot be summoned using the standard summoning spells. Time elementals attack by forming misty or smoky arms from their forms and lashing at opponents or by spraying a fine mist onto their opponents so as to induce aging. Against particularly powerful opponents, a time elemental uses its alter age ability or (if of the royal sort) summons additional time elementals to its aid.","credit":"The Time Elemental originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Sand Giant","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["earth","giant"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+3 armor, +1 Dex, +12 natural, -2 size","hp":218,"hd":"19d8+114 (+19)","hdvalue":19,"fort":17,"ref":7,"will":9,"defensive_abilities":["rock catching"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"greatsword +24 (4d6+16) or 2 slams +23 (2d6+11)","ranged":"rock +14 (2d6+16)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fist of sand","details":"slam +26, 1d8+10 damage; DC 29; CMB +26, CMD 36; AC 20, touch 8, flat-footed 20; hp 69; 19 rounds"},{"type":"rock throwing","details":"120 ft."}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":19,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":25,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"earthquake"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"move earth"},{"spell":"soften earth and stone"}]}],"strength":33,"dexterity":13,"constitution":23,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":12,"charisma":14,"baseatk":14,"cmb":27,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","cmd":38,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (greatsword)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Survival","value":23}],"languages":["Common","Giant"],"sq":[{"type":"weapon and armor proficiency"}],"environments":["warm deserts"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-4)","raiding party (6-9 plus 1 cleric or sorcerer of 6th-9th level)","family (2-4 plus 35% noncombatants)","tribe (8-27 plus 35% noncombatants and 1 sorcerer of 10th-12th level and 1 cleric of 9th-11th level)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This giant looks like a savage humanoid with dark tan skin, dark hair, and green eyes.","group":"Giant","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fist of Sand","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day as a move action, a sand giant can form a volume of sand within 40 ft. into the shape of a 20-foot long arm that ends in a clenched fist. The arm is Huge and has a space of 15 ft. and a reach of 20 ft. The arm and fist cannot move from the location where it was created. The sand giant can order the arm to attack a target as a move action. Once given a target, the arm automatically attacks that target on the giant's turn. The arm remains for a number of rounds equal to the sand giant's Hit Dice (19 rounds for a typical sand giant). A sand giant doesn't need to concentrate to maintain the arm and can direct it to attack a new target or adapt a new tactic as a free action. The arm's base attack bonus is equal to that of the giant that created it, and it deals slam damage equal to the slam attack for a creature of its size (Huge). Any creature struck must succeed on a DC 29 Fortitude save or be stunned for 1 round. The save DC is Strength-based, using the HD of the sand giant and the Strength of the fist of sand. The arm has an AC of 20 (+12 natural, -2 size) and has hit points equal to three times the Constitution score of the sand giant that created it. It has a Strength score of 30. The arm loses shape if it is reduced to 0 or less hit points, the duration expires, or the sand giant dies."},{"type":"Weapon and Armor Proficiency","kind":"Ex","details":"Sand giants are automatically proficient with simple weapons, martial weapons, light and medium armor, and shields."}],"description":"Sand giants are brutal, somewhat barbaric giants that prey on those weaker than themselves. They have dark tan skin, brown hair, and dark brown or dark green eyes. An adult male stands approximately 20 ft. tall. Males tend to wear their hair and beards braided. Sand giants wear light clothes and light armor (if any). In times of battle or war, males may don chainmail. A typical sand giant's bag contains food, 3d4 mundane items, and a modest amount of cash (no more than 12d10 coins). Sand giants can live to be 500 years old. Sand giants make their homes in warm desert lands away from civilization. They live in organized tribes consisting of 8-9 families of 2-4 members each.\n\nOn occasion, a tribe forms a raiding party that sets off to the nearest civilized place, returning at a later time with food, coins, and captives. For each adult in a sand giant's lair, there is a 40% chance that the lair has 1d3 captives of any humanoid race. Sand giants favor their greatswords in combat. They usually begin combat by shaping a fist from the surrounding terrain and attacking with their greatswords in concert with the earthen fist. Sand giant don't throw rocks like many other giants do, but they can catch rocks or similar projectiles as other giants.","as_character":[{"description":"Sand giants are combative, and most are fighters. Many tribes or groups include druids or clerics with access to two of the following domains Earth, Evil, Strength, and War.","racial_traits":[{"type":"Ability Score Bonuses","value":"+22 Strength, +2 Dexterity, +12 Constitution, +2 Intelligence, +2 Wisdom, +4 Charisma."},{"type":"Huge","value":"Sand giants are Huge and take a -2 penalty to AC, -2 penalty to attack rolls, +2 bonus to Combat Maneuver Bonus and Combat Maneuver Defense, and a -8 penalty to Stealth checks. A sand giant's lifting and carrying limits quadruple those of Medium characters. Space 15 ft., Reach 15 ft."},{"type":"Speed","value":"A sand giant's base speed is 50 ft."},{"type":"Low-light vision","value":"Sand giants can see twice as far as humans in conditions of dim light."},{"type":"Racial Hit Dice","value":"A sand giant starts with nineteen levels of humanoid, which provide it with 19d8 HD, a base attack bonus of +14, and base save bonuses of Fort +11, Ref +6, Will +6."},{"type":"Racial Skills","value":"A sand giant's giant levels give it skill points equal to 19 x (2 + Int modifier). Its class skill are Intimidate and Perception."},{"type":"Racial Feats","value":"A sand giant's giant levels give it 10 feats."},{"type":"AC","value":"+12 natural AC bonus."},{"type":"Special Attacks","value":"Fist of sand, spell-like abilities."},{"type":"Special Qualities","value":"Rock catching, scent."},{"type":"Weapon and Armor Proficiency","value":"Sand giants are automatically proficient with simple weapons, martial weapons, light and medium armor, and shields."},{"type":"Languages","value":"Sand giants begin play speaking Giant and Common. Sand giants with high intelligence scores can choose from the following languages: Draconic, Elven, Goblin, and Orc."}]}],"gear":"greatsword, studded leather armor"},{"name":"Very Old Gray Dragon","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","init":4,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"smoke vision"}],"auras":["frightful presence (270 ft., DC 22)"],"ac":36,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":36,"ac_mods":"+28 natural, -2 size","hp":237,"hd":"19d12+114","hdvalue":19,"fort":17,"ref":13,"will":17,"dr":"15/magic","immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":25,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"average"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +27 (2d6+10), bite +28 (2d8+15/19-20), 2 wings +25 (1d8+5), tail slap +25 (2d6+15)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, 18d6 fire; DC 25 Ref half"},{"type":"pyroclast"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":19,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":25,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"ash storm"},{"spell":"burning hands"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"},{"spell":"steal breath"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":9,"spellsknown_concentration":15,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"cloudkill"},{"spell":"telekinesis"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"dimension door"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"scrying"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"gaseous form"},{"spell":"protection from energy"},{"spell":"ray of exhaustion"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"eagle's splendor"},{"spell":"gust of wind"},{"spell":"locate object"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"burning hands"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"protection from good"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shield"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"acid splash"},{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"ray of frost"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"touch of fatigue"}]}],"strength":31,"dexterity":10,"constitution":23,"intelligence":17,"wisdom":19,"charisma":17,"baseatk":19,"cmb":31,"cmd":41,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":25},{"skill":"Fly","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":30},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":30},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":25},{"skill":"Stealth","value":14},{"skill":"Swim","value":40}],"languages":["Aquan","Common","Draconic","Giant Special Abilities"],"sq":[{"type":"adaptive breathing"}],"environments":["warm coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"Steam emanates from the nostrils and mouth of this slate gray dragon.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Adaptive Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A gray dragon does not require respiration, and is immune to effects that require breathing (such as inhaled poison). This ability does not grant immunity to cloud or gas attacks that do not require breathing."},{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A gray dragon's breath weapon is a superheated line of steam."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older gray dragon can take any animal or humanoid form 3/day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Pyroclast","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older gray dragon can use its breath weapon to create a cloud of volcanic smoke and ash as a standard action that deals fire damage equal to the dragon's hit dice to any creature inside it. The cloud moves with the dragon and has a radius of 20 feet and lasts 3d4 rounds. Any creature that starts its turn inside the cloud takes damage, but can make a Reflex save for half. A strong wind, such as that created by a gust of wind, disperses the cloud in 1 round."},{"type":"Smoke Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young gray dragon can see perfectly in smoky conditions (such as those created by pyrotechnics)."},{"type":"Sooty Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"Living creatures that fail their saves against the gray dragon's breath weapon are tormented by burning eyes. This effect imposes a -4 penalty to AC and a -2 penalty on attack rolls for 2d4 rounds."}],"description":"Gray dragons are evil dragons that inhabit mountains and hills near coastlines. They have little regard for other races and often enslave others to do their bidding. Adult and older gray dragons are rarely found without a retinue of humanoid slaves. Gray dragons mate for life and a single mated pair often terrorizes nearby villages, laying waste to those that oppose the dragon's will."},{"name":"Volcano Giant","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CN","size":"Huge","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["earth","fire","giant"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":29,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+2 armor, +1 Dex, +18 natural, -2 size","hp":201,"hd":"20d8+120","hdvalue":20,"fort":18,"ref":7,"will":9,"defensive_abilities":["rock catching"],"immunities":["fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"Gargantuan longspear +24 (4d6+16, crit x3) or 2 slams +24 (2d6+11)","ranged":"rock +15 (2d6+16 plus 1d6 fire)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon"},{"type":"rock throwing","details":"120 ft."},{"type":"trample","details":"2d6+16; DC 31"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":26,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"stone shape"}]}],"strength":32,"dexterity":12,"constitution":23,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":14,"charisma":11,"baseatk":15,"cmb":28,"cmd":39,"feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":14,"special":"+18 jumping"},{"skill":"Climb","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":18}],"languages":["Giant","Ignan"],"sq":[{"type":"oversized weapon use"}],"environments":["warm mountains"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-5)","band (6-9 plus 35% noncombatants plus 1 adept or cleric of 1st or 2nd level)","hunting/raiding party (6-9 plus 1 adept or sorcerer of 3-5th level plus 3-8 fire lizards)","tribe (21-30 plus 1 adept, cleric, or sorcerer of 6th or 7th level plus 12-30 fire lizards)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This 18-foot tall, barrel-chested giant has leathery, reddish brown skin and haunting amber eyes. The creature is tough and wiry, with the strength and texture of copper.","group":"Giant","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day, a volcano giant can exhale a cloud of warm and sulfuric gas in a 30-foot cone. Affected creatures must make a successful DC 26 Fortitude save or take a -4 circumstance penalty on attack rolls, checks and saves for 1 minute (10 rounds) due to fits of coughing and choking. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Oversized Weapon Use","kind":"Ex","details":"A volcano giant wields a Gargantuan two-handed longspear without penalty."}],"description":"Volcano giants make their homes in the many twisting caves and subterranean rooms of volcanic cones, enlarging and reinforcing them for comfort and convenience. Clothing for a volcano giant usually consists of little more than a simple wrap of fire lizard skin. A volcano giant wears ornaments made of bone, shell, and obsidian, and their general culture and society is similar to that of humanoid civilizations on tropical islands. Such island societies often get along well with local tribes of volcano giants, engaging in trade and peacefully coexisting. Should a tribe of volcano giants form an allegiance with a human tribe, the giants warn the humans of possible eruptions of their volcano to allow them time to escape the destruction.\n\nAlthough volcano giants can be described as good-natured and peaceful people, their demeanor can change quickly. At a real or imagined affront, a volcano giant can erupt with a passion that is rivaled only by the fire and fury of the volcano in which it lives. Volcano giants feel that their shadow is actually their soul, and don't tolerate any creature that dares to trod upon it. Volcano giants usually use Gargantuan longspears in combat. They are fierce and brave warriors, not backing down from any adversary. Many choose to open combat with their breath weapon so as to soften up their foes before attacking.","as_character":[{"racial_traits":[{"type":"Ability Score Bonuses","value":"+22 Strength, +2 Dexterity, +12 Constitution, +2 Wisdom: A volcano giant's prowess lies almost entirely in his physical abilities, predominantly strength."},{"type":"Huge","value":"Volcano giants are huge and take a -2 penalty to AC, -2 penalty to attack rolls, +2 bonus to Combat Maneuver Bonus and Combat Maneuver Defense, and a -8 penalty to Stealth checks. A volcano giant's lifting and carrying limits quadruple those of Medium characters. Space 15ft., Reach 15ft."},{"type":"Speed","value":"A volcano giant's base speed is 40 ft."},{"type":"Low-light vision","value":"volcano giants can see twice as far as humans in conditions of dim light."},{"type":"Racial Hit Dice","value":"A volcano giant starts with seventeen levels of giant, which provide it with 20d8 HD, a base attack bonus of +15, and base save bonuses of Fort +12, Ref +6, Will +6."},{"type":"Defensive Abilities","value":"a volcano giant gains the rock catching defensive ability."},{"type":"Racial Skills","value":"A volcano giant's giant levels give it skill points equal to 20 x (2 + Int modifier). Its class skills are Acrobatics, Climb, Intimidate, Knowledge (nature), and Perception."},{"type":"Racial Feats","value":"A volcano giant's giant levels give it ten feats."},{"type":"AC","value":"Tough-skinned, volcano giants gain a +18 natural AC bonus."},{"type":"Special Attacks","value":"Breath weapon, rock throwing, trample."},{"type":"Spell-like Abilities","value":"volcano giants can cast stone shape 1/day as a 20th level caster."},{"type":"Special Qualities","value":"fire and earth subtypes, low-light vision, oversized weapon use,"},{"type":"Automatic Languages","value":"Giant, Ignan. Volcano giants with high Intelligence scores can choose from the following languages: Draconic, Goblin, Terran, Orc."}]}],"gear":"Gargantuan longspear, leather armor"},{"name":"Vorin","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"aberration","init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +6 natural, -2 size","hp":178,"hd":"17d8+102","hdvalue":17,"fort":11,"ref":9,"will":10,"dr":"15/slashing or piercing","immunities":["acid"],"resists":[{"type":"fire","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"sting +20 (2d6+9 plus poison), bite +19 (2d6+9)","ranged":"spit +15 (poison)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"spit"}],"strength":28,"dexterity":18,"constitution":23,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":11,"charisma":12,"baseatk":12,"cmb":23,"cmd":37,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (sting)"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Stealthy"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (spit)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (sting)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":6},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":2},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13,"special":"+21 in water"}],"sq":[{"type":"water breathing"}],"environments":["any marshes"],"organizations":["solitary","squad (2-5)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature is an immense greenish-black thing with intense yellow eyes. It is 30 ft. long and a foot thick. The body of the thing is a wormlike mass of pulpy flesh with several gill-like apertures along its length with which it propels itself through the water. The front of the beast has a long trunk similar to that of an elephant. Its skin glistens as if coated with a sheen of oil.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite or spit-injury or contact; save Fort DC 24; frequency 1/round for 2 rounds; effect 1d6 Dex and paralyzed 1d4 hours; cure 1 save. The save DC is Constitution-based. An opponent struck by a blob of vorin poison spit at them is protected from its effects for a short time by any amount of worn armor—the blob strikes the armor but not the opponent's flesh. The blob of poison seeps through armor in a number of rounds equal to the armor's armor bonus (don't apply any magical bonuses). The blob can be scraped off as a move action. Natural armor doesn't provide any defense as the poison seeps through the opponent's pores, nor does poison delivered by a vorin's sting have the same delayed effect."},{"type":"Spit","kind":"Ex","details":"Once per round a vorin can spit a blob of sticky poison with a sickening odor at a single opponent within 50 ft. (no range increment). This requires the vorin to make a successful ranged touch attack. If struck, a target is subjected to the vorin's poison."},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"Vorins can breathe underwater indefinitely."}],"description":"Vorins live in dismal swamps and bogs, lurking down in the murk and the mire. The eyes of a vorin are raised above the rest of the head on slight bulges. This arrangement allows the vorin to remain mostly submerged while it watches its potential prey. A typical vorin is 30 ft. long and weighs 3,000 pounds.\n\nThe boneless body of a vorin helps to protect it from impacts. A vorin feeds and attacks with a long proboscis. This proboscis contains the creature's tongue, with is tipped with a thorny barb that can inject a paralytic poison. A vorin can also spit its poison at prey that it can't reach physically.\n\nA vorin relies on its poison in combat, hoping to incapacitate an opponent so it can consume the victim at its leisure. It enters combat by spitting poison at any larger opponents first. The vorin tries to remain at a distance, spitting its poison and darting back below the water to slither to another location before rising again. A vorin only enters melee if pressed or if it is unable to escape."},{"name":"Willow Dusk","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"plant","init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +20 natural, -2 size","hp":210,"hd":"20d8+120","hdvalue":20,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":17,"ref":7,"will":9,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["plant traits"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"4 slams +23 (2d8+9 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"aura of misery"},{"type":"droning"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"2d6+9 plus 1d8 acid damage, AC 19, 21 hp"}],"strength":29,"dexterity":8,"constitution":21,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":16,"charisma":10,"baseatk":15,"cmb":26,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. trip, +4 vs. grapple","cmd":35,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (aura of misery)"},{"feat":"Ability Focus (droning)"},{"feat":"Improved Trip"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":23},{"skill":"Stealth","value":6,"special":"+22 in forests"}],"languages":["Sylvan"],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"You see a 20 foot tall willow tree with dark greenish-brown branches and blackish-brown bark.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Aura of Misery","kind":"Su","details":"Once every 1d4+1 rounds as a free action, a willow dusk can emit a wave of negative energy that affects all living creatures within 10 ft. of it. Creatures within the area take 1d6 points of Charisma damage if they fail a DC 22 Will save. At Charisma 0, a creature collapses into a coma until at least 1 point of Charisma is restored. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Droning","kind":"Su","details":"Once per round as a standard action, a willow dusk can emit a droning sound audible to a range of 100 ft. Creatures within the area that hear it, must succeed on a DC 22 Will save or enter a state of lethargy. Affected creatures cannot move (as if held by a hold monster spell) and have no desire to take any other action or engage in combat (unless attacked first, in which case the lethargy effect is broken). The effects last for a number of rounds equal to the one-half of the willow dusk's Hit Dice (10 rounds for the typical willow dusk). A willow dusk that attacks a creature affected by this ability gains a +4 bonus on its attack roll. Whether the attack succeeds or fails, the lethargy effect is immediately broken. A creature who succeeds on his Will save is unaffected by the droning from that same willow dusk for 24 hours. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Willow dusks are nocturnal predators that drone their targets into a lethargic state or a coma-induced sleep before relentlessly attacking and devouring them. To the untrained eye, a willow dusk appears as a normal willow tree and nothing more. Any creature with 5 or more ranks in Knowledge (nature) or Survival can detect \"something's not quite right about that tree\" on a successful DC 20 check.\n\nA willow dusk prefers to devours a victim whole, scooping it up in its massive branches and dumping it fully into its gaping maw where its stomach acids digest its swallowed prey. Willow dusks prefer warmblooded creatures to cold-blooded creatures and always eat freshly killed prey. They are not scavengers and will not eat something they didn't kill (or at least something that has been dead longer than 1 hour).\n\nA willow dusk appears as a 20-foot tall willow tree and can grow to a height of 40 ft. or more. A typical willow dusk is 20 ft. tall and weighs 900 pounds.\n\nOccasionally, willow dusks have been known to aid evil-aligned druids and rangers.\n\nA willow dusk hunts at night, just as the sun is setting. When it finds a potential victim, it looses its droning and charges an opponent who succumbs to its effect, bashing it with a slam attack or grappling it and tossing it into its maw. Creatures who resist the willow dusk's droning are subjected to its aura of misery attack as long as they remain within 10 ft. of the creature. An opponent that falls to Charisma 0 is quickly scooped up by the willow dusk and devoured."},{"name":"Zombie Horde","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Colossal","type":"undead","subtypes":["horde"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":13,"ac_touch":2,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+11 natural, -8 size","hp":110,"hd":"20d8 (+20)","hdvalue":20,"fort":6,"ref":6,"will":12,"defensive_abilities":["half damage from piercing weapons"],"dr":"10/slashing","immunities":["undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"horde attack (6d6)","space":"30 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"feral rage"},{"type":"rend","details":"+3d6"}],"strength":22,"dexterity":10,"wisdom":10,"charisma":10,"baseatk":15,"cmb":29,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Overrun","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Toughness","type":"bonus"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Stealth","value":-16}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","mass (2-4 hordes)","apocalypse (5+ hordes)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A stumbling crush of moaning, reaching bodies comes towards you. Empty eyes seek you out, each staggering footstep bringing the deathless mass closer. Straining to grasp you, this group of zombies are so tightly packed together it seems to be a single mass of undead, flailing limbs.","group":"Horde","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Feral Rage","kind":"Ex","details":"The horde attacks as a ruthless mob, intent only on tearing apart those that fall into their clutches. This frenzy prevents them from using any sort of tactics, and frees them from any form of control by other beings. However, the sheer force of the wave attack allows them to deal 6d6 points of damage to any creature whose space they occupy at the end of their move. This ability is lost if the horde is broken up."},{"type":"Horde Traits","kind":"Ex","details":"Hordes are not so called because of the size of the group but rather the size of the creatures that compose the horde. Unlike normal swarms, hordes are composed of Medium creatures which are usually a normal version of a creature but otherwise behave in a swarmlike manner. There are usually around 50 creatures in a horde. The net effect is that they take only half damage from piercing weapons but take normal damage from other weapons. In addition when the swarm is reduced to 0 hit points or lower and breaks up, unless the damage was dealt by area-affecting attacks, then 2d6 surviving members of the horde continue their attack, though now only as individual creatures. Otherwise, a horde conforms to all of the other swarm traits. Rend (EX) Due to the grasping and clawing nature of the zombie horde attack, any time the horde does more than 20 points of damage, add 3d6 slashing damage from the additional pulling and tearing. This ability is lost if the swarm is broken up."}],"description":"Zombies are one of the most used and abused of the mindless undead. Singly, a zombie may be dealt with by experienced adventurers. When gathered together in a horde, these mindless creatures are a terror to behold. Packed together as tightly as they are, they appear as one solid mass of decaying flesh and sinuous limbs.\n\nThe flailing nature of the zombie horde's limbs allow the throng to grasp and tear at opponents, dealing rend damage in addition to their base attack. Any time the horde is in an opponent's square, the target risks being completely overrun by the horde If the horde takes enough individual damage to break it up, up to a dozen of the creatures continue on their rampage of destruction, until finally they too must be slain.","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk (© Frog God Games, 2012)"},{"name":"Ancient Gray Dragon","cr":15,"xp":51200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","init":4,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"smoke vision"}],"auras":["frightful presence (300 ft., DC 24)"],"ac":39,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":39,"ac_mods":"+31 natural, -2 size","hp":283,"hd":"21d12+147","hdvalue":21,"fort":19,"ref":14,"will":19,"dr":"15/magic","immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":26,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"average"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +30 (2d6+11), bite +31 (2d8+16/19-20), 2 wings +28 (1d8+5), tail slap +28 (2d6+11)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, 20d6 fire; DC 27 Ref half"},{"type":"pyroclast"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":21,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":28,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"ash storm"},{"spell":"burning hands"},{"spell":"pyrotechnic eruption"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"},{"spell":"steal breath"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":11,"spellsknown_concentration":18,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":6,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"flesh to stone"},{"spell":"move earth"}]},{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"cloudkill"},{"spell":"telekinesis"},{"spell":"transmute rock to mud"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dimension door"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"scrying"},{"spell":"stoneskin"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"gaseous form"},{"spell":"protection from energy"},{"spell":"ray of exhaustion"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"eagle's splendor"},{"spell":"gust of wind"},{"spell":"locate object"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"burning hands"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"protection from good"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shield"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"acid splash"},{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"ray of frost"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"touch of fatigue"}]}],"strength":33,"dexterity":10,"constitution":25,"intelligence":19,"wisdom":21,"charisma":19,"baseatk":21,"cmb":34,"cmd":44,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":28},{"skill":"Fly","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":33},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":33},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":28},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16},{"skill":"Swim","value":43}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aquan","Common","Draconic","Giant Special Abilities"],"sq":[{"type":"adaptive breathing"},{"type":"smoke form"}],"environments":["warm coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"Steam emanates from the nostrils and mouth of this slate gray dragon.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Adaptive Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A gray dragon does not require respiration, and is immune to effects that require breathing (such as inhaled poison). This ability does not grant immunity to cloud or gas attacks that do not require breathing."},{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A gray dragon's breath weapon is a superheated line of steam."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older gray dragon can take any animal or humanoid form 3/day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Pyroclast","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older gray dragon can use its breath weapon to create a cloud of volcanic smoke and ash as a standard action that deals fire damage equal to the dragon's hit dice to any creature inside it. The cloud moves with the dragon and has a radius of 20 feet and lasts 3d4 rounds. Any creature that starts its turn inside the cloud takes damage, but can make a Reflex save for half. A strong wind, such as that created by a gust of wind, disperses the cloud in 1 round."},{"type":"Smoke Form","kind":"Ex","details":"An ancient or older gray dragon can assume a smoky form as a move action, once per day. It can spend up to 1 minute per day per HD in smoke form. This time does not have to be consecutive, but it must be spent in 1-minute increments. A smoke form dragon can fly at its normal fly speed (but good maneuverability). The ability is otherwise similar to a gaseous form spell."},{"type":"Smoke Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young gray dragon can see perfectly in smoky conditions (such as those created by pyrotechnics)."},{"type":"Sooty Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"Living creatures that fail their saves against the gray dragon's breath weapon are tormented by burning eyes. This effect imposes a -4 penalty to AC and a -2 penalty on attack rolls for 2d4 rounds."}],"description":"Gray dragons are evil dragons that inhabit mountains and hills near coastlines. They have little regard for other races and often enslave others to do their bidding. Adult and older gray dragons are rarely found without a retinue of humanoid slaves. Gray dragons mate for life and a single mated pair often terrorizes nearby villages, laying waste to those that oppose the dragon's will."},{"name":"Beluiri (The Temptress)","cr":15,"xp":51200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"true seeing"}],"ac":40,"ac_touch":25,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +1 dodge, +15 natural, +7 profane","hp":184,"hd":"16d10+96","hdvalue":16,"fort":16,"ref":14,"will":17,"dr":"15/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":26,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +22 (1d6+6 plus poison)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"dominating gaze"},{"type":"seduction"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":26,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"true seeing"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"deeper darkness"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect law"},{"spell":"fear"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"polymorph self"},{"spell":"tongues","details":"self only"},{"spell":"unhallow"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"fire storm"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 1d4 hezrous or 1d4 gharros demons, 100%"},{"spell":"wail of the banshee"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]}],"strength":22,"dexterity":24,"constitution":22,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":20,"charisma":24,"baseatk":16,"cmb":22,"cmd":47,"feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (seduction)"},{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":18},{"skill":"Bluff","value":30},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":26},{"skill":"Disguise","value":27},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":26},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":36},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":28},{"skill":"Stealth","value":26},{"skill":"Survival","value":21}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Goblin","Infernal"],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Beluiri plus 1d4 hezrous or 1d4 gharros demons)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature appears as a bronze-skinned female standing about 6 ft. tall. Its head is hairless and features four downward-curving horns jutting just above its forehead. The two lower horns are smaller than the topmost horns. A ridge of small spines runs from the creature's brow down the center of its head and tapers off just below its shoulder blades. Its hands end in razor-sharp talons and its eyes are sapphire blue.","group":"Demon Lord","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Dominating Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day, 30 ft., DC 25 Will save or dominated as per the dominate person spell (CL 20th). The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Claw-injury; save Fort DC 24; frequency 1 round for 4 rounds; effect 1d4 Str damage; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Seduction","kind":"Su","details":"Through body language and movement, Beluiri can fascinate all creatures of the opposite sex (which could be either sex, depending on her current form) within 30 ft. that observe her dancing. Those viewing this dance must succeed on a DC 27 Will save or fall under her influence for 1d6+1 hours as if affected by a charm monster spell (CL 20th). The save DC is Charisma-based and includes a +2 bonus from her Ability Focus feat."}],"description":"Beluiri is one of the many concubines of Lord Baphomet (and one of his favorites). She is known throughout the Abyss as the Temptress, for in her many disguises she has seduced countless princes, lords, and generals of the Abyss. In the end, she most often betrays those that fall victim to her wiles. She is hated for this by more than one noble or lord of the Abyss. She sometimes journeys to the Material Plane (in one of her many guises) to tempt and seduce mortals, for she knows that all mortals, in their hearts, always give in to their true desires-be it power, greed, lust, or one of many countless other sins.\n\nBeluiri rarely wears clothing, but at times when she does, she enjoys gowns and robes of gold, white, and red.\n\nBeluiri prefers subterfuge rather than directly assaulting an opponent.\n\nShe usually alters her appearance to appear as an attractive member of a potential victim's race; once the victim is lured in, she assumes her true form and attacks. If combat goes against her, she flees, but only after summoning lesser demons to cover her escape and kill her opponents."},{"name":"Cat Lord","cr":15,"xp":51200,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["native","shapechanger"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"200 ft."},{"type":"detect evil"},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"keen senses"},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":32,"ac_touch":20,"ac_flat_footed":25,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +12 natural, +3 insight","hp":199,"hd":"19d10+95","hdvalue":19,"fort":16,"ref":20,"will":7,"defensive_abilities":["feline passivism","immortality"],"dr":"20/magic and cold iron","immunities":["mind-affecting effects","psionics"],"sr":26,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"climb","speed":30}],"melee":"2 claws +27 (1d6+7 plus grab), bite +26 (1d8+7)","ranged":"spit +26 (blindness)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"howl"},{"type":"pounce"},{"type":"rake","details":"2 claws +27, 1d6+7"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":19,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":24,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect evil"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"speak with animals","details":"felines only"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"hypnotism"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"astral projection"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"ethereal jaunt"},{"spell":"haste","details":"self only"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 6, 1d4+2 lions or tigers, or 1d4+4 leopards or cheetahs, or 1d2 dire lions, dire tigers, or weretigers, or 30 + 1d20 normal cats 100%"}]},{"frequency":"9/day","spells":[{"spell":"dimension door"},{"spell":"lick wounds","details":"self only; heals 2d4 damage"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":25,"constitution":20,"intelligence":19,"wisdom":17,"charisma":20,"baseatk":19,"cmb":17,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":34,"feats":[{"feat":"Acrobatic"},{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Athletic"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claws)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":38,"special":"+50 when jumping"},{"skill":"Climb","value":38},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":26},{"skill":"Fly","value":9},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":24},{"skill":"Heal","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":23},{"skill":"Perception","value":29},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":29},{"skill":"Stealth","value":37},{"skill":"Survival","value":22},{"skill":"Swim","value":9}],"languages":["Common","Sylvan","Druidic","Elven","Goblin","Gnome","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"change shape","details":"human and panther, polymorph"}],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Cat Lord plus 3-6 lions or tigers, or 5-8 cheetahs)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature resembles a great black panther with ruby eyes.","group":"Cat Lord","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"The Cat Lord can assume the shape of a human as a standard action. In human form, the Cat Lord cannot use his natural weapons or his howl, pounce, spit, or rake special attacks but can wield weapons and wear armor. Unlike the normal change shape ability, the Cat Lord retains his movement modes (and speeds) in human form."},{"type":"Feline Passivism","kind":"Ex","details":"Felines (including dire versions) don't willingly attack the Cat Lord, though they can be forced to do so by magic. If the Cat Lord attacks a feline, its protection against that creature ends."},{"type":"Howl","kind":"Su","details":"When the Cat Lord howls, all creatures except felines within a 20-foot spread must succeed on a DC 24 Will save or be stunned for 1d2 rounds. A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by the Cat Lord's howl for one day. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Immortality","kind":"Su","details":"The Cat Lord is effectively immortal and nearly impossible to slay. When slain, the Cat Lord's soul reforms on the Astral Plane. Within 9 days, it inhabits another feline on the Material Plane and the Cat Lord reforms. No form of magic (such as magic that would contain or trap his soul) prevents this. To permanently kill the Cat Lord, it is thought that one must destroy every feline in existence (so his soul has no creature to inhabit)."},{"type":"Keen Senses","kind":"Ex","details":": The Cat Lord sees five times as well as a human in shadowy illumination and normal light."},{"type":"Spit","kind":"Ex","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds as a ranged attack, the Cat Lord can spit a line of caustic saliva at a single target to a range of 30 ft. A creature hit must succeed on a DC 24 Reflex save or be blinded. Remove blindness or dispel magic (vs. CL 19th) removes the blindness effect. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"There is only one. The Cat Lord is the Lord of All Felines. His natural form is that of a black panther with dark, ruby eyes. He can assume a human form, and in this form, he appears as a dark-skinned human with black hair, chiseled features, and ruby eyes. In human form, he stands 6 ft. tall and he almost always dresses in black. The Cat Lord spends his days roaming the Material Plane, Astral Plane, and Ethereal Plane.\n\nIn combat, the Cat Lord almost always assumes feline form (if he's not already in that form) and attacks with two claws and a bite. The Cat Lord often enters combat with both haste and blur in effect. If combat goes against him, he usually summons a group of felines to his aid or to cover his escape.","credit":"The Cat Lord originally appeared in Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Crysolax","cr":15,"xp":51200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["scintillating aura (20 ft.; DC 20 Will)"],"ac":27,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +16 natural, -2 size","hp":172,"hd":"15d10+90","hdvalue":15,"fort":17,"ref":12,"will":7,"dr":"10/magic and bludgeoning","immunities":["blindness","light-based effects"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":26,"weaknesses":["vulnerable to sonic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"2 claws +22 (1d8+8/19-20 plus grab), bite +21 (2d6+8 plus 1d6 Dex damage)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"petrifying bite"},{"type":"scintillating aura"}],"strength":27,"dexterity":16,"constitution":22,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":14,"charisma":16,"baseatk":15,"cmb":25,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":38,"cmd_special":"+12 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (petrifying bite)"},{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":21},{"skill":"Climb","value":26},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":24},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":4},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13},{"skill":"Survival","value":20}],"languages":["Common","Terran"],"environments":["any (Plane of Earth)"],"organizations":["solitary","carat (2-4)"],"treasure":"incidental coins and items; twice standard gemstones","description_visual":"This creature looks like a horrible amalgam of a centipede and a praying mantis made out of translucent white crystal with brilliant multifaceted blue eyes.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Petrifying Bite","kind":"Ex","details":"The bite of a crysolax deals 1d6 points of Dexterity damage. A creature reduced to Dex 0 is turned to crystal (as the stone to flesh spell) permanently if it fails a DC 25 Fortitude save. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +2 bonus from the crysolax's Ability Focus feat."},{"type":"Scintillating Aura","kind":"Ex","details":"As long as there is a light source present within 30 ft. of it, the crysolax constantly radiates an aura that duplicates the effects of a rainbow pattern spell (CL 15th). The save is Charisma-based."}],"description":"A terrifying predator native to the Plane of Earth (and also a pocket dimension known as the Demiplane of Crystal), the crysolax is a hunter, active most often during the daylight hours. During the day, natural sunlight refracts from the crysolax causing it to appear to be a multitude of different colors. It uses this natural sunlight to activate its aura when hunting or in combat.\n\nA crysolax spends its days hunting creatures native to the Plane of Earth, while at night, the creature is usually found in its lair, a large and complex maze of twisting corridors, caverns, and spiraling tunnels located deep within the rocky earth of its native plane. A crysolax lair usually consists of 2-4 adults and twice that number in smaller noncombatant crysolax. The female lays 4-8 large crystal eggs usually once per year. These eggs usually hatch within 60 days and a crysolax reaches maturity within two years. Its lair is also scattered with any treasure it may have gathered. Though not a creature known for collecting treasure, a crysolax is quite fond of gemstones, and as such a large amount of said treasure usually can be found in its lair. While a crysolax has no need to eat, some do enjoy ingesting certain gemstone (the exact type seems to vary between each crysolax).\n\nA crysolax attacks with its bite, attempting to petrify the strongest opponents first. It also rakes and slashes with its razor-sharp claws or grabs a foe and repeatedly subjects it to its bite attack, knowing that eventually the victim will succumb to its petrifying nature."},{"name":"Empyreal","cr":15,"xp":51200,"alignment":"LG","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["angel","extraplanar","good","lawful"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect evil"},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"auras":["aura of goodness","protective aura"],"ac":27,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +14 natural, -1 size | +4 deflection vs. evil","hp":136,"hd":"13d10+65","hdvalue":13,"fort":15,"ref":12,"will":8,"save_mods":"+4 vs. poison, +4 vs. evil","dr":"10/evil","immunities":["acid","cold","petrification","death effects"],"resists":[{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":26,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":70,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+3 flaming longsword +23 (1d8+10 plus 1d6 fire)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"radiant blast"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":13,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":18,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect evil"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"aid"},{"spell":"continual flame"},{"spell":"discern lies"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"holy smite"},{"spell":"invisibility","details":"self only"},{"spell":"plane shift"},{"spell":"remove curse"},{"spell":"remove disease"},{"spell":"remove fear"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"heal"},{"spell":"raise dead"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"blade barrier"},{"spell":"cure serious wounds"},{"spell":"flame strike"},{"spell":"scorching ray","details":"3 rays"}]},{"frequency":"5/day","spells":[{"spell":"cure moderate wounds"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":18,"constitution":20,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":18,"charisma":20,"baseatk":13,"cmb":21,"cmd":35,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (longsword)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":21},{"skill":"Fly","value":22},{"skill":"Heal","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":17},{"skill":"Perception","value":28},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16},{"skill":"Survival","value":20}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic","Infernal","truespeech"],"environments":["any good-aligned plane"],"organizations":["solitary","group (2-4)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature resembles a man-sized column of white fire. Within the burning fires seems to be a winged humanoid-shaped creature dressed in shining armor.","group":"Angel","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Aura of Goodness","kind":"Su","details":"An empyreal radiates an aura in a 30-foot radius spread around its form. Any non-evil creature in this area must succeed on a DC 23 Will save or be overcome with awe and unable to attack the empyreal that round. Evil creatures within the area must make a successful DC 23 Will save or be unable to even look at that empyreal for one day. An affected evil creature functions as if blinded (as the blindness spell) when attacking that empyreal. On a successful save, a creature is immune to the aura of goodness of that empyreal for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based and includes a +2 bonus."},{"type":"Radiant Blast","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day, an empyreal can increase the radiance of its form and release it in a cone-shaped blast to a range of 60 ft. that deals 15d6 points of damage and blinds any creature in the area (as the blindness spell) for 3d6 minutes. Affected creatures can make a successful DC 21 Reflex save to halve the damage and avoid being blinded. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Empyreals are knights and warriors in the service of good deities. While closely associated with other angels, empyreals are often found leading holy armies against the forces of evil. They are fiery, quick-tempered, and forceful, but always fair.\n\nIn the upper planes those that serve as commanders spend their time organizing their troops and planning strategies. While the more powerful empyreals serve as commanders, the lesser can be found performing any number of duties, whether it is acting as guard, servant, or messenger.\n\nEmpyreals that enter combat prefer to attack their opponents with a mixture of magic and direct physical attacks with their longswords. Against powerful foes, an empyreal uses its radiant blast to catch as many foes as it can in the area of effect. During battle, an empyreal often stays aloft where it can blast its foes with spells while staying out of melee range.","gear":"+3 flaming longsword"},{"name":"Fisherman","cr":15,"xp":51200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["aquatic","evil","lawful","native"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"deathwatch","modifier":"15 miles"},{"type":"weather sense","modifier":"30 miles"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":202,"hd":"15d10+120","hdvalue":15,"fort":13,"ref":11,"will":16,"dr":"15/magic","immunities":["cold"],"resists":[{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":26,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"swim","speed":30}],"melee":"+3 boat hook +26 (1d8+13) or +3 boat hook +22 (1d8+9), +3 boat hook +22 (1d6+9) or +3 boat hook +22 (1d8+9), +3 gaff hook +22 (1d8+9)","ranged":"net +16 (entangle)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":23,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"deathwatch","details":"15 mile radius"},{"spell":"freedom of movement","details":"underwater"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon nature's ally V"}]}],"spellsprepared_caster_level":9,"spellsprepared_concentration":17,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"slay living","count":2}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"control water"},{"spell":"spell immunity"},{"spell":"unholy blight"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"bestow curse"},{"spell":"deeper darkness"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"water walk"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"align weapon"},{"spell":"darkness"},{"spell":"death knell"},{"spell":"enthrall"},{"spell":"silence"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"bane"},{"spell":"command"},{"spell":"curse water","count":2},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"sanctuary"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"bleed"},{"spell":"create water"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"mending"}]}],"strength":28,"dexterity":15,"constitution":26,"intelligence":15,"wisdom":21,"charisma":20,"baseatk":15,"cmb":25,"cmd":37,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Two-Weapon Fighting"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":23},{"skill":"Craft (any)","value":20},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":23},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":23},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":23},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":23},{"skill":"Swim","value":35}],"languages":["Aquan","Sylvan"],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"},{"type":"create soul cage"},{"type":"exotic weapons"},{"type":"gambling"}],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard (+3 boat hook, +3 gaff hook, net)","description_visual":"This large humanoid stands over 10 ft. tall, and is clad in the garb of a mundane fisherman. Its eyes glow with an eerie blue light and its grizzled face is trimmed with a gnarled beard from which scuttle small crabs, fish, and shrimp.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Create Soul Cage","kind":"Su","details":"Using debris that floats to the bottom of the ocean, a fisherman can construct a soul cage. The soul cage is a magical construction that, through its crafting, has been endowed with a trap the soul spell. The spell requires no material components other than the debris from which it is created. The magic of the soul cage only functions for fishermen and the souls remain trapped for as long as the fisherman wishes and remains on the Material Plane. Usually, only upon the death of the fisherman may the trapped souls be released. A soul cage can hold up to six souls at any given time."},{"type":"Deathwatch","kind":"Sp","details":"A fisherman makes constant use of the spell deathwatch, as cast by a 15th level cleric. The range of a fisherman's deathwatch is 1 mile per hit die, allowing it to sense the life state of any creature within its territory. This ability can be negated, but the fisherman can reactivate it the next round as a free action."},{"type":"Exotic Weapons","kind":"Ex","details":"A fisherman is proficient in the use of the boat hook and gaff hook."},{"type":"Gambling","kind":"Ex","details":"Fishermen are fond of games and gambling and should one be offered a fair chance of odds, he may find a wager impossible to resist. In this way, it may be possible to bargain for the release of the soul of a companion or loved one. Although evil, fishermen are bound by a personal code and honor the terms of a wager if they lose. Spells Fishermen cast divine spells as 9th-level clerics. They don't gain access to domains or other cleric abilities."},{"type":"Weather Sense","kind":"Su","details":"A fisherman always knows the condition of the weather within a 30 mile radius, even if he is currently underwater."}],"description":"The fisherman is a rare creature not often encountered by the mortals of the material world. Sages and scholars often postulate these boathooks, gaff hooks, and nets to ensnare and slay those who intrude upon their habitat. All fishermen seem to be male—no female of the species has ever been witnessed by any sailor. They are powerful creatures who enjoy tormenting seafarers and work hard to collect the souls of those who die at the hands of the sea. At the bottom of the ocean they may be found tending to devices called soul cages that resemble ordinary lobster traps, though they are used to imprison the spirits of the drowned. The territory of a fisherman can extend over a dozen miles from its lair.\n\nFishermen stand between 11 and 12 ft. tall and weigh 1,600 pounds.\n\nWhen a fisherman detects a great storm at sea, or is otherwise aware that sailors are meeting watery deaths, it rises to the surface in order to start collecting as many of the souls as it can. An individual fisherman may tend to as many as 3d6 soul cages, each containing the incarcerated spirits of 1d6 unfortunate sailors, all of which have met their deaths through storm, shipwreck, or some other maritime disaster. Those slain by intentional violence are left to wander the depths by the fisherman. They are very competitive with others of their kind but occasionally they swap souls to enhance their own collections.\n\nSpecial Weapons\n\nBoat Hook: A boat hook resembles a quarterstaff with a barbed hook at one end. Sailors use boat hooks to snag mooring lines and pull in small boats. Because a boat hook isn't intended to be used as a weapon, it requires the Exotic Weapon Proficiency to be used in that capacity. A boat hook is a double weapon. The damage is given as hook/staff.\n\nCost 6 gp; Small 1d4/1d3, Medium 1d6/1d4, Large 1d8/1d6; Critical x2; Weight 5 lb.; Type Bludgeoning/Piercing.\n\nGaff Hook: A gaff hook is a curved metallic hook with a cross bar. Gaff hooks are used by fishermen to lift heavy catches into their boats. Because a gaff hook isn't intended to be used as a weapon, it requires the Exotic Weapon Proficiency to be used in that capacity.\n\nCost 4 gp; Small 1d4, Medium 1d6, Large 1d8; Critical x2; Weight 3 lb.; Type Piercing."},{"name":"Herald Of Tsathogga","cr":15,"xp":51200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"aberration","subtypes":["chaotic","evil","extraplanar"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +16 natural, -2 size","hp":231,"hd":"22d8+132","hdvalue":22,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, fire)"],"fort":12,"ref":12,"will":18,"dr":"10/good","resists":[{"type":"sonic","value":15}],"weaknesses":["bloated"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"swim","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +21 (2d6+7 plus grab), 10 tentacles +20 (1d8+3 plus paralysis), tongue +20 (1d6+3 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (30 ft. with tongue)","special_attacks":[{"type":"bellow"},{"type":"paralysis","details":"1d6+4 rounds, DC 26"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"2d6+7 plus 2d6 acid damage, AC 18, 23 hp"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":16,"constitution":20,"intelligence":7,"wisdom":16,"charisma":12,"baseatk":16,"cmb":25,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":38,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (tentacle)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (tongue)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Intimidate","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":34},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15},{"skill":"Swim","value":19}],"environments":["warm marshes"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature appears to be a gigantic pale yellow-green frog with oversized monstrous eyes. In place of its legs and forelimbs are many long, writhing tentacles it uses to pull itself along the ground.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Bellow","kind":"Su","details":"A herald of Tsathogga has two distinct bellows, each usable once every 1d4 rounds. The first is a trilling croak like that of a frog. All opponents with 30 ft. hearing this trilling must succeed on a DC 22 Fortitude save or be deafened for 1d6+4 rounds. Opponents within 10 ft. must make a DC 22 Fortitude save or be stunned for 1d4 rounds. Alternately, a herald can focus its bellow attack against a single opponent within 100 ft. The opponent takes 5d6 points of sonic damage. A successful DC 22 Reflex save reduces the damage by half. The save DCs are Charisma-based."},{"type":"Bloated","kind":"Ex","details":"Because of its bloated, heavy body, a herald of Tsathogga that attacks with more than 5 tentacles in one round cannot move that round."},{"type":"Regeneration","kind":"Ex","details":"A herald of Tsathogga takes normal damage from fire and good-aligned weapons, and from spells or effects with the good descriptor."}],"description":"The dark, dismal tropical swamps and fens of the world are home to a horrible creature known only as the herald of Tsathogga. A vaguely froglike thing almost 20 ft. across, the herald of Tsathogga is a nightmare creature that is spoken of only in hushed whispers. The creature is believed to have been created by the Frog God as punishment against humanity for wrongdoings done to Tsathogga and his worshippers.\n\nIts warty, putrid skin is a pale yellow-green, and two monstrous eyes that have seen unknown secrets gaze from its fleshy face. The body of the thing resembles that of a massive toad, but rather than legs the herald of Tsathogga drags itself through the murky terrain on ten thick tentacles.\n\nThese tentacles are covered in tiny lancets that inject paralytic venom.\n\nSome who have seen the herald of Tsathogga swear that it is capable of flight, but these reports are dismissed as madman's fantasy.\n\nThough only one herald is thought to exist, rumors as of late, speak of at least three of these creatures in existence.\n\nA herald of Tsathogga attacks first with its tentacles, attempting to paralyze or otherwise incapacitate as many opponents as possible.\n\nParalyzed opponents are pulled to the creature's maw and bitten. Its tentacles are not coordinated enough to grab moving targets, so it cannot pick up opponents that have not been paralyzed."}];
